      "writtenOn": "2021-11-04T17:06:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Jumping in on this thread. I\u0027m not really sure I understand the concern. Having explicit register names and sizes isn\u0027t a bad thing and will likely reduce bugs. Having an array of uint8_t for all the registers is much more prone to bugs when you start accessing 2+ byte registers. Regardless, in an array you\u0027re still relying on some kind of name by doing something like `reg[INT_STATUS_1]` vs `int_status_reg1` so you\u0027re not really saving any raw code size.\n\nAs a side note:\nDatasheets are usually out of date, OEMs don\u0027t maintain them well. The emulator needs to model the actual chip behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "c02e22c9_12d5ed19",
      "revId": "ae0ee78260c79f5d1c538fbd39b864dd79e3e679",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b6ff75a_366a15e7",
        "filename": "zephyr/emul/emul_sn5s330.c",
