      "writtenOn": "2021-11-05T03:02:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see what you mean, but I think that the key aspect to the model this emulator is following is that it\u0027s easy to update (which happens a lot). Since the datasheet isn\u0027t up-to-date, we often find out about quirks 5+ CLs after we write a branch (such as `write reg X`). We then have to account for a bunch of side-effects in that `case` statement. Having things split up (while uses a lot of boilerplate) makes the future CLs much easier to diff and easier to understand.",
      "parentUuid": "5b6ff75a_366a15e7",
      "revId": "ae0ee78260c79f5d1c538fbd39b864dd79e3e679",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
